  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Monday)\nIssued at 1145 AM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nToday has been a dry day with cooler than normal temps, a nice\nbreak from the heat. The fly in the ointment has been the wildfire\nsmoke that is blowing in from the west, causing hazy skies and\nthe local air quality index to reach Moderate for most of the\narea. Some localized spots have reported the index reaching\nUnhealthy for Sensitive Groups.\n\nFor tonight, the wildfire smoke will linger. Overnight temps will\ndip into the 40s to near 50 for most of the area. Any precip\nchances are found mainly in NE WY into SW SD where some upper\nlevel energy could get some light showers going. Hi-res models\nhave been scaling back on the chances so this part of the forecast \nmay get updated and removed with the late evening update. Stay\ntuned.\n\nWednesday is looking like a dry day with afternoon highs below \nnormal for early August, only reaching the upper 70s to mid 80s. \nWinds will be generally on the lighter side, about 5 to 10 mph, \nout of the south. The main concern will be wildfire smoke \nlingering over the area through Wednesday night. And if the upper\nwinds remain out of the west, the smoke forecast could be\nstretched into Thursday.\n\nFor Thursday and Friday, upper level ridging looks to return to\nthe area, which will bring warmer temps and continued dry weather.\nDaily highs will be in the upper 80s to 90s and overnight lows\nwill be in the 50s to low 60s.\n\nThe 90s and dry weather will last through the weekend with hints\nof slightly cooler weather for the start of next week.",
